# Test code inherits the project .clang-tidy and relaxes two checks.
# cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes: GoogleTest fixtures
# expose their state as protected members so TEST_F bodies, which derive from the
# fixture, can reach it. That is the framework's own idiom.
# bugprone-random-generator-seed: a deterministic test seeds its engine with a
# fixed constant on purpose, so the result is reproducible run to run. That is the
# whole point of this chapter, so the check does not apply to test code (production
# code, which should seed from a real entropy source, still gets it).
# Both still apply to the shipping library under src/.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -bugprone-random-generator-seed
